WEBVTT

1
00:00:22.291 --> 00:00:23.958
<b>In the previous several verses,</b>

2
00:00:23.958 --> 00:00:26.958
<b>Lord Krishna explained the true </b>
<b>meaning of sacrifice</b>

3
00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:31.875
<b>and described how performing sacrifices </b>
<b>leads to the purification of a person.</b>

4
00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:32.541
<b>Now,</b>

5
00:00:32.541 --> 00:00:34.458
<b>in this verse, Lord Krishna explains</b>

6
00:00:34.458 --> 00:00:37.208
<b>what will happen if one does</b>
<b>not perform sacrifices.</b>

7
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.333
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna says</b>

8
00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:47.291
<b>that those who do not participate</b>
<b>in these sacrifices</b>

9
00:00:47.291 --> 00:00:51.333
<b>do not attain happiness in this world or life.</b>

10
00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:53.875
<b>And if this is the case in this birth itself,</b>

11
00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:57.541
<b>then the question of happiness in the </b>
<b>next birth does not even arise.</b>

12
00:00:57.541 --> 00:01:00.291
<b>As we have also understood </b>
<b>in the previous verses,</b>

13
00:01:00.291 --> 00:01:04.875
<b>here the reference to sacrifice </b>
<b>represents selfless renunciation.</b>

14
00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:11.500
<b>A renunciation that leads to the purification</b>
<b>of the soul and towards spiritual goals.</b>

15
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:18.666
<b>Here, renunciation means voluntarily </b>
<b>giving up or donating any object,</b>

16
00:01:18.666 --> 00:01:26.083
<b>whether it is the donation of time, labor, </b>
<b>wealth, or something else. </b>

17
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:30.750
<b>Its main purpose is to give up something </b>
<b>of your own for others,</b>

18
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.958
<b>because only this brings true satisfaction.</b>

19
00:01:33.958 --> 00:01:35.041
<b>On the other hand,</b>

20
00:01:35.041 --> 00:01:41.500
<b>people who live only for their own pleasure </b>
<b>and self-interest, without the spirit of sacrifice,</b>

21
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.291
<b>always remain dissatisfied in life.</b>

22
00:01:44.291 --> 00:01:48.666
<b>Happiness does come into their lives too, </b>
<b>but it does not last.</b>

23
00:01:48.666 --> 00:01:51.250
<b>Satisfaction is also momentary,</b>

24
00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.708
<b>not permanent.</b>

25
00:01:52.708 --> 00:01:54.750
<b>Because people who run after...</b>

26
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:59.041
<b>hoarding happiness, wealth, and prosperity </b>
<b>only for themselves,</b>

27
00:01:59.041 --> 00:02:05.541
<b>their lives slowly begin to become hollow </b>
<b>due to the fear of losing these very things.</b>

28
00:02:05.541 --> 00:02:09.000
<b>Sacrifice is necessary not</b>
<b>only for spiritual progress </b>

29
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:15.041
<b>but also for a meaningful and</b>
<b>balanced worldly life.</b>

30
00:02:15.041 --> 00:02:20.000
<b>Lord Krishna had given a similar message </b>
<b>in the third chapter as well.</b>

31
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.333
<b>Where the matter was of selfless </b>
<b>action, of the welfare of others.</b>

32
00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:29.375
<b>Performing actions selflessly for </b>
<b>the welfare of others</b>

33
00:02:29.375 --> 00:02:32.708
<b>became a kind of donation of labor and time,</b>

34
00:02:32.708 --> 00:02:35.291
<b>or you could say it became a sacrifice.</b>

35
00:02:35.291 --> 00:02:38.000
<b>Lord Krishna's core message is</b>

36
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.750
<b>that sacrifice or renunciation is the</b>
<b>foundation of a meaningful life.</b>

37
00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:45.958
<b>Whether it is through selfless actions,</b>

38
00:02:45.958 --> 00:02:51.500
<b>faithful fulfillment of duty, or devotion to God.</b>

39
00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.791
<b>Sacrifice purifies the soul</b>

40
00:02:53.791 --> 00:02:56.416
<b>and paves the way for liberation.</b>

41
00:02:56.416 --> 00:02:59.833
<b>Without it, happiness remains distant in this life</b>

42
00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:02.083
<b>and in the life to come.</b>

43
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.958
<b>Humans are running,</b>

44
00:03:08.958 --> 00:03:13.041
<b>engaged in hoarding material</b>
<b>pleasures and means.</b>

45
00:03:13.041 --> 00:03:14.541
<b>He thinks that</b>

46
00:03:14.541 --> 00:03:19.500
<b>he is the master of these </b>
<b>material pleasures, independent,</b>

47
00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:28.000
<b>but the irony is that he unwittingly </b>
<b>becomes a prisoner of these things.</b>

48
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.791
<b>Think about it,</b>

49
00:03:29.791 --> 00:03:39.166
<b>if you get irritated by the loss or snatching </b>
<b>of a valuable object and happiness goes away,</b>

50
00:03:39.166 --> 00:03:44.083
<b>was your happiness independent?</b>

51
00:03:44.083 --> 00:03:47.541
<b>Or was it under the control of that object?</b>

52
00:03:47.541 --> 00:03:53.500
<b>True happiness is freedom from </b>
<b>these materialistic things.</b>

53
00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:59.458
<b>And this is the significance of renunciation.</b>

54
00:03:59.458 --> 00:04:05.041
<b>Because if you have learned selfless sacrifice,</b>

55
00:04:05.041 --> 00:04:13.000
<b>then in a way you have automatically </b>
<b>cut the shackles bound by materialism.</b>

56
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.500
<b>And if the shackles are cut,</b>

57
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:20.166
<b>then the mind will also fly freely like a bird.</b>

58
00:04:20.166 --> 00:04:23.208
<b>One will have to move slowly forward on this path.</b>

59
00:04:23.208 --> 00:04:27.708
<b>The mind that has been absorbed in </b>
<b>materialism and selfishness so far</b>

60
00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:30.916
<b>will have to be slowly freed.</b>

61
00:04:30.916 --> 00:04:35.500
<b>And this beginning can also </b>
<b>be made with small steps.</b>

62
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.458
<b>For example,</b>

63
00:04:37.458 --> 00:04:40.666
<b>the time you spend on this phone </b>
<b>for entertainment or</b>

64
00:04:40.666 --> 00:04:47.416
<b>looking at others' lives on social media,</b>

65
00:04:47.416 --> 00:04:53.083
<b>the beginning can be made</b>
<b>by sacrificing that time.</b>

66
00:04:53.083 --> 00:05:02.708
<b>This personal progress, mental and physical </b>
<b>strength will give your mind lasting satisfaction.</b>

67
00:05:02.708 --> 00:05:04.041
<b>Looking at it,</b>

68
00:05:04.041 --> 00:05:13.916
<b>it is like renouncing materialism and moving </b>
<b>towards a higher purpose and spiritual progress.</b>

69
00:05:13.916 --> 00:05:20.833
<b>Discipline for higher purposes, </b>
<b>this too is a sacrifice.</b>

70
00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:22.666
<b>Try following it,</b>

71
00:05:22.666 --> 00:05:25.708
<b>you will experience extreme happiness.</b>

72
00:05:30.083 --> 00:05:36.625
<b>Sacrifice or renunciation in the family </b>
<b>environment is not only a necessity,</b>

73
00:05:36.625 --> 00:05:37.750
<b>but</b>

74
00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:43.083
<b>it is the complete basis of family happiness.</b>

75
00:05:43.083 --> 00:05:48.041
<b>You are still making this sacrifice </b>
<b>or renunciation in the family,</b>

76
00:05:48.041 --> 00:05:51.291
<b>there is just no awareness of it.</b>

77
00:05:51.291 --> 00:05:52.250
<b>So</b>

78
00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:58.750
<b>recognize the family sacrifices and then </b>
<b>follow them consciously.</b>

79
00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.208
<b>Think,</b>

80
00:06:00.208 --> 00:06:04.166
<b>when someone comes home tired </b>
<b>from work in the evening,</b>

81
00:06:04.166 --> 00:06:11.000
<b>but their child or a family member wants </b>
<b>to tell something with great enthusiasm,</b>

82
00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.083
<b>then in such a situation</b>

83
00:06:12.083 --> 00:06:19.625
<b>that person sacrifices his desire for rest </b>
<b>and dedicates his time to the family.</b>

84
00:06:19.625 --> 00:06:24.291
<b>Even this seemingly small thing is a sacrifice.</b>

85
00:06:24.291 --> 00:06:26.791
<b>Similarly, family members</b>

86
00:06:26.791 --> 00:06:31.708
<b>sacrifice their entertainment programs </b>
<b>for the sake of others' preferences.</b>

87
00:06:31.708 --> 00:06:34.916
<b>They give their time to help others.</b>

88
00:06:34.916 --> 00:06:41.000
<b>This too was like sacrificing a part </b>
<b>of one's life for someone else.</b>

89
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:46.541
<b>Society is also an extended form of family, isn't it?</b>

90
00:06:46.541 --> 00:06:54.750
<b>So if you now start making this sacrifice </b>
<b>for others apart from family members,</b>

91
00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:59.416
<b>then in a way your family is expanding,</b>

92
00:06:59.416 --> 00:07:06.666
<b>love is spreading, your relationships with </b>
<b>others are becoming sweeter.</b>

93
00:07:06.666 --> 00:07:08.333
<b>And yes,</b>

94
00:07:08.333 --> 00:07:13.000
<b>sacrificing ego is also a sacrifice.</b>

95
00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:19.500
<b>When you apologize for a mistake, or many </b>
<b>times even when there is no mistake,</b>

96
00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:23.875
<b>when you take the first step to resolve a quarrel,</b>

97
00:07:23.875 --> 00:07:31.916
<b>then it is a sacrifice of ego for a </b>
<b>higher purpose, it is a sacrifice.</b>

98
00:07:31.916 --> 00:07:37.541
<b>Know this spirit of sacrifice, follow it.</b>

99
00:07:37.541 --> 00:07:41.000
<b>It will not only bring family peace</b>

100
00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.000
<b>but</b>

101
00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:48.375
<b>also spiritual prosperity </b>
<b>to everyone in the family.</b>

102
00:07:48.375 --> 00:07:51.625
<b>This is the door to lasting happiness.</b>

103
00:07:51.625 --> 00:07:53.333
<b>Reflect upon this.</b>

104
00:07:57.791 --> 00:08:04.583
<b>Sacrifice in the professional environment</b>
<b>is never a sacrifice of one's values.</b>

105
00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:08.541
<b>Rather, it is recognizing those opportunities</b>

106
00:08:08.541 --> 00:08:14.666
<b> where you can make some personal </b>
<b>sacrifices for collective progress.</b>

107
00:08:14.666 --> 00:08:17.208
<b>And this principle of sacrifice</b>

108
00:08:17.208 --> 00:08:23.791
<b>deeply affects both personal success </b>
<b>and the progress of the organization.</b>

109
00:08:23.791 --> 00:08:25.166
<b>Think</b>

110
00:08:25.166 --> 00:08:33.250
<b>an organization whose members occasionally </b>
<b>sacrifice their comfort when needed</b>

111
00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:36.291
<b>and lend a hand in collective goals.</b>

112
00:08:36.291 --> 00:08:43.000
<b>Even after their personal work is completed, </b>
<b>they help their colleagues</b>

113
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.458
<b>so that everyone progresses.</b>

114
00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:47.250
<b> On the other hand, someone else,</b>

115
00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:52.416
<b>being experienced, automatically </b>
<b>chooses difficult tasks.</b>

116
00:08:52.416 --> 00:09:00.250
<b>Because he knows that this will help both </b>
<b>the organization and his colleagues.</b>

117
00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.833
<b>Leaving behind the desire for momentary gain,</b>

118
00:09:02.833 --> 00:09:04.916
<b>abandoning the easy path,</b>

119
00:09:04.916 --> 00:09:12.916
<b>and walking the difficult but right path for the </b>
<b>goals of the organization and values of an ideal life</b>

120
00:09:12.916 --> 00:09:16.125
<b>this too is a sacrifice of renunciation.</b>

121
00:09:16.125 --> 00:09:19.583
<b>There are many opportunities for </b>
<b>sacrifice in professional life.</b>

122
00:09:19.583 --> 00:09:24.000
<b>The need is only to recognize these opportunities</b>

123
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:29.375
<b>and then, leaving aside personal interest, </b>
<b>to fulfill one's duty</b>

124
00:09:29.375 --> 00:09:32.458
<b>and help others.</b>

